<BaseLayout title="Research Updates & Evidence Changes" description="A dated record of important Standby Generator Guide research changes, unresolved source conflicts and planning-tool methodology updates."><article class="editorial-container publication-section prose-hgg"><h1>Research updates</h1><p>This log records material editorial changes. It does not imply professional review or that every older article was reverified.</p><h2>October 8, 2026 — homeowner decisions and operational checks</h2>
<ul><li>Added a faster three-question path to sizing, real installed costs and exact-model comparisons without replacing the detailed research workflow.</li><li>Introduced conditional, source-conscious buyer checks on brand and model pages and direct links to official manufacturer service locators.</li><li>Published a blank private-use quote worksheet; the original-research project still has zero verified submissions and no open intake.</li><li>Documented the priority review brief while retaining the disclosure that no independent licensed review has been completed.</li><li>Removed an orphaned duplicate Cloudflare build trigger unrelated to the active staging Worker, preserving the real Worker build and GitHub QA.</li></ul>
<h2>October 5, 2026 — planning platform</h2><ul><li>Expanded the exact-model library to 31 configurations across five manufacturers, including ATS package variants. Added field-level source maps and explicit missing fields.</li><li>Added four browser tools for load planning, fuel scenarios, three-quote comparison and ownership budgets. Assumptions and calculation limits appear with each tool.</li><li>Withheld disputed Generac 10 kW fuel-output/weight fields and Champion 26 kW sound figures rather than resolving manufacturer contradictions by assumption.</li><li>Marked KOHLER 26RCA ATS scope and 26RCA/26RCAL weight discrepancies for clarification.</li><li>Added selected Generac and KOHLER manual-based service schedules, a printable log and Fairfax County’s official permit starting point.</li><li>Added reviewer infrastructure. No professional reviewer or completed licensed review has been recorded.</li></ul><p><a href="/source-policy/">Source policy</a> · <a href="/corrections-policy/">Request a correction</a></p></article></BaseLayout>
